diff --git a/tests/NATIVE_SPLIT.md b/tests/NATIVE_SPLIT.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ec077c33
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/NATIVE_SPLIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Native Split Checks
+
+Build normally with Meson, then run `meson test -C build --print-errorlogs`.
+`native_geometry` covers exact placement, the 640-pixel local minimum,
+panel-sized usable bounds, negative origins, overflow, fixed hints, output
+availability, scaling, and conflicting reservations. `native_reservation`
+drives the production state machine with scene/protocol doubles, including
+configure acknowledgement, an already-sized neutral buffer, hint transitions,
+workspace release/return, conflict rejection, buffer mismatches, output
+revocation, overview suspension (including mapping during overview), DPMS
+sleep/wake recovery, and unmap.
+
+`native_prediction` runs the production horizontal and vertical scroller cores
+without a compositor. It checks the 1478-pixel local region, arrangement/prediction
+agreement, reserved-client exclusion, unchanged reservation state during probes,
+fullscreen origins with panel offsets, and restoration of the saved layout and
+workarea. These unit tests do not verify
+live rendering, input coordinates, or physical-pixel capture.
+
+## Isolated Integration
+
+Never run these checks on a live desktop. Create a private `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`,
+unset `DISPLAY` and `WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, use `WLR_BACKENDS=headless` and
+`WLR_HEADLESS_OUTPUTS=1`, and pass Mango a separate configuration. Compile
+`headless-output.c` with `cc -shared -fPIC -ldl` and preload it for that Mango
+process only to name the initial output `DP-2`. Scenefx requires a working
+render node; software-only initialization is not supported by every build.
+
+Use these test rules with zero gaps, border width 2, and animations disabled:
+
+```
+monitor_rule=name:DP-2,scale:1,x:0,y:0,width:3398,height:1440,refresh:60
+tag_rule=id:1,layout_name:tile
+window_rule=app_id:^com\.linuxmis\.linuxmis$,title:^Linuxmis Native Stream$,monitor:DP-2,is_floating:0,no_border:1,no_swallow:1,reserve_right:1
+```
+
+Set **both** the test client's `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` and `MANGO_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE`
+to the private compositor. `mmsg` uses `MANGO_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE`, not just
+`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`. Map an SDL client with equal positive min/max size hints,
+present a neutral buffer, and query `get all-clients`. Accept only an explicit
+`reservation.status == "accepted"` before presenting video. A neutral buffer
+already at the requested size does not require another configure/commit.
+
+At 1920x1080, verify `(1478,180)` and two local clients each occupying 739
+pixels on the left. Capture a black/white single-pixel-column test pattern and
+compare all 2073600 stream pixels. Check 1920x1440 and 2758x1440 acceptance,
+2759x1440 and 1920x1441 rejection, blocked resize/floating/fullscreen/group
+actions, second-stream rejection, workspace return, and tile-layout restoration
+after close. Disable the private output with an accepted client paused to
+verify its retained `rejected/output_unavailable` IPC record before it handles
+the close event. Stop only the private compositor and remove its runtime.
